{"number": 159, "text": "                     5  Hilary Benn, a British politician, has filled me with admiration over the last five years. | think he is\n                        principled and intelligent, which is not something that can be said about all politicians.\n                     6  | take more pride in my work, if, by home, you mean the house that | live in. But if by home you\n                        mean  family, then | take more pride in my home.\n                        | feel great love for my husband, my son and my nephews.\n                     ~“\n                     8  | personally get more pleasure from reading.\n\n\n                     Unit  60\n             60.1    1  standing         5 richly/justly      9  singing\n                     2  thunderous       6 won               10 justly/richly\n                     3  acclaim          7 take              11  offer\n                     4  warmly           8 gives             12  round\n             60.2    1T\n                     2  F-  If you have nothing but praise for someone, you praise them a lot and have no criticisms to\n                        make  of them.\n                        F - If you criticise someone roundly, you criticise them very strongly.\n                     DS W\n                        1\n                        F - If you counter criticism, you criticise your critic back.\n                        F - lf someone gives their blessing to something, they say they are in favour of it.\n\n                        +\n\n             60.3       He came  in for a lot of criticism.\n                        | thoroughly disapprove of how she responded to the criticism.\n                        The judge severely condemned  him / condemned  him severely for lying.\n                        | want to express my disapproval of her behaviour.\n                        The critics were outspoken but he dismissed their criticisms.\n                        His comments  received universal condemnation.\n                        We strenuously objected to the plan and were highly critical of it.\n                        Or We were  highly critical of the plan and strenuously objected to it.\n                     8  | have always been a harsh critic of corrupt government.\n             60.4         is the last exercise in this book. May we give you a pat on the back for getting to this point.\n                      Indeed, you richly/justly deserve a big clap. We have nothing but praise for you and would like to\n                      offer you our warm congratulations!\n\n\n                                                                      English Collocations in Use Intermediate    157", "char_count": 2654, "mean_conf": 92.35, "word_count": 330, "words": [{"text": "5", "x0": 434, "y0": 222, "x1": 452, "y1": 251, "conf": 84, "bold": false}, {"text": "Hilary", "x0": 487, "y0": 218, "x1": 597, "y1": 260, "conf": 89, "bold": false}, {"text": "Benn,", "x0": 612, "y0": 220, "x1": 718, "y1": 258, "conf": 96, "bold": false}, {"text": "a", "x0": 732, "y0": 228, "x1": 750, "y1": 251, "conf": 96, "bold": false}, {"text": "British", "x0": 766, "y0": 219, "x1": 886, "y1": 252, "conf": 96, "bold": false}, {"text": "politician,", "x0": 901, "y0": 219, "x1": 1088, "y1": 260, "conf": 96, "bold": false}, {"text": "has", "x0": 1103, "y0": 219, "x1": 1166, "y1": 252, "conf": 96, "bold": false}, {"text": "filled", "x0": 1180, "y0": 218, "x1": 1271, "y1": 252, "conf": 96, "bold": false}, {"text": "me", "x0": 1287, "y0": 228, "x1": 1344, "y1": 252, "conf": 95, "bold": false}, {"text": "with", "x0": 1356, "y0": 218, "x1": 1437, "y1": 251, "conf": 96, "bold": false}, {"text": "admiration", "x0": 1452, "y0": 218, "x1": 1659, "y1": 251, "conf": 96, "bold": false}, {"text": "over", "x0": 1674, "y0": 227, "x1": 1756, "y1": 251, "conf": 96, "bold": false}, {"text": "the", "x0": 1767, "y0": 218, "x1": 1828, "y1": 251, "conf": 96, "bold": false}, {"text": "last", "x0": 1843